red its lease/route again, confirming the corrected persistent state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-62ff18310764404c","cmd-f83a6e2c8ccd4ffc","cmd-bf1d6c05de2a4222","cmd-88010a0d1b9148d0","cmd-a82b7177af584cad","cmd-4695802b613c42c4","cmd-e484826d092341ca","cmd-7e991cbce136402b","cmd-f0f5974b8ce44ecf","cmd-9fce40cdef53444f"]},{"id":"clients-dynamic-addressing","requirement":"node3 and node4 obtain addressing from the router in front of them rather than from static configuration","status":"satisfied","summary":"node3 and node4 each had no prior static configuration on their lan-facing interface (eth1); the executor created persistent NetworkManager DHCP profiles (ipv4.method auto) on eth1 for each, which acquired addresses/routes from their respective routers and, critically, re-acquired the same addressing automatically after a full reboot with no executor re-configuration, confirming the DHCP client config (not static) is what drives addressing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-509b364e46514d3b","cmd-a82b7177af584cad","cmd-3d9d4b41b7c94485","cmd-f8a57424366b4c63"]},{"id":"node-restart-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on all four managed nodes (independent of public task contract)","status":"satisfied","summary":"All four nodes show a pre-restart boot identity/health capture, a restart acknowledgement, a distinct post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/data/route state: node1 (Kea + lease + eth2 intact, node3 reachable), node2 (Kea clean after re-applying the persistent dnsmasq fix, lease intact, node4 reachable), node3 (auto DHCP reacquisition, route, ping), node4 (auto DHCP reacquisition, route, ping). This is cross-checked against the fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot, which independently shows all four boot identities changed relative to before-prepare.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9b9101aeae2049f2","cmd-7b7390539fe4420e","cmd-841e0df5941b4590","cmd-ce2f6fcefe8345fd","cmd-75ef2da147c94b1b","cmd-0af4639d2dbb44d7","cmd-1863be55f3